# Test: `ze <verb> <path>` reaches the daemon, the offline fallback, and the
# accept-only: the registered native fixture enforces this scenario's behavioral contract
#       subcommand list, each with the right exit code.
#
# VALIDATES: a command argv (`ze show log levels`) resolves against the
#            verb-relative command tree and dispatches on the ABSOLUTE path the
#            daemon is keyed on; a trailing positional value (`ze show log
#            recent count 5`) reaches the handler that owns it; `ze show host`
#            answers with the daemon UP and with it DOWN; `ze show bgp peer`
#            lists its members and exits 1.
# REGRESSION: cmdutil.RunCommand walked cli.BuildVerbCommandTree, which is
#            RELATIVE to the verb, with the ABSOLUTE argv words. 56 of the 63
#            `ze show` commands answered `unknown command`. Nothing caught it:
#            every `exec=ze show ...` test in this suite landed on a local
#            handler, an offline fallback, or the bare-verb help page, so none
#            drove a daemon-dispatched subcommand through the verb form.
#            The first repair then read `show host` as a bare grouping container
#            and printed a subcommand list instead of running the fallback.
#            The second repair keyed the value tail on ArgDefs, so declared
#            commands whose YANG declares no leaf still answered `unknown
#            command` through the verb form while `ze cli -c` ran the same
#            words. Checks 10 to 13 pin the two resolvers together and keep the
#            local-handler namespace out of the daemon's path boundary. Check
#            14 covers a short local handler swallowing commands declared below
#            it.
#
# The daemon runs with an ephemeral SSH listener; ZE_SSH_* carry the credentials
# the verb form has no flags for.
#
# The timeout is declared rather than derived. One daemon start plus the command
# launches runs in about 8s on an idle host, while parallel agents have slowed
# the suite by 3.5x without invalidating any assertion.
option=timeout:value=120s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture ui/cli-verb-daemon-dispatch
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
